e posedge at 15ns (`a=0` at that posedge) and `0` after the posedge at 45ns (`a=1`), i.e. `q` is the **inversion of `a` delayed by one clock cycle**: `q(N) = ~a(N-1)`. The current DUT registers `a` then inverts it, creating a two-cycle delay, so `q` stays `x` a cycle too long (first mismatch at 20ns). Fix: a single register sampling `~a`."}},{"type":"block-end","index":2,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_b4xAEBVuAfckt3PlmJCM8516","name":"edit_dut","arguments":"{\"expected_revision_id\": \"3e017af9-f452-4930-a429-ff27f1a7df43\", \"source\": \"module TopModule (\\n    input  clk,\\n    input  a,\\n    output reg q\\n);\\n\\n    always @(posedge clk) begin\\n        q <= ~a;\\n    end\\n\\nendmodule\\n\"}"}},{"type":"usage","usage":{"inputTokens":4672,"outputTokens":323,"totalTokens":6147,"cacheReadTokens":1152,"reasoningTokens":70}},{"type":"finish","reason":{"kind":"tool-calls"}}]